n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(1-4)^{2}+(2-4)^{2}+(4-4)^{2}+(9-4)^{2} \\\\  & =9+4+0+25 \\\\  & =38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm = \\dfrac{-26}{38} = -\\dfrac{13}{19} \\approx -0.7.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =3-(-\\frac{13}{19})\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{109}{19} \\\\  & ≈5.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny = -0.7x + 5.7.\n$$" 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096595 1071 "| **Years ($x$)** | $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Value ($y$)** | **$35$** | **$26$** | **$19$** | **$16$** |\n\nThe table above gives the value of a car a few years after it was purchased (in thousands of dollars). You are given that $\\overline{x}=2$ and $\\overline{y}=24.$ Find the equation of the corresponding linear regression line and use this to predict how long it takes for the car's value to drop to $\\[math]10\\,000.$ Round your answer to the nearest year." 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096595 1071 "| **Years ($x$)** | $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| **Value ($y$)** | **$35$** | **$26$** | **$19$** | **$16$** |\n\nThe table above gives the value of a car a few years after it was purchased (in thousands of dollars). You are given that $\\overline{x}=2$ and $\\overline{y}=24$. Find the equation of the corresponding linear regression line and use this to predict how long it takes for the car's value to drop to $\\[math]10\\,000$. Round your answer to the nearest year." 13194139535987 17592186045417 false] [17592186096595 1074 "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny = mx+b\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{S_{xy}}{S_{xx}}, b = y^(―) - mx^(―)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m{:}$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n$S_{xy}|= ∑_(i = 1)^(n)(x_{i} - x^(―))(y_{i} - y^(―)); = (0 - 2)(35 - 24) + (1 - 2)(26 - 24); = + (3 - 2)(19 - 24) + (4 - 2)(16 - 24); = (-2)(11) + (-1)(2) + (1)(-5) + (2)(-8); =-22 - 2 - 5 - 16; =-45$\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n$S_{xx}|= ∑_(i = 1)^(n)(x_{i} - x^(―))^{2}; = (0 - 2)^{2} + (1 - 2)^{2} + (3 - 2)^{2} + (4 - 2)^{2}; = 4 + 1 + 1 + 4; = 10$\n- Now, substituting into the formula for $m$, we obtain\n$m =-\\dfrac{45}{10} = -4.5$.\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nb &= y^(―) - mx^(―) \\\\\n&= 24 - (-\\frac{9}{2}) \\cdot 2 \\\\\n&= 33\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny = -4.5x+33\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate the required value by substituting $y=10$ into the equation of the trend line and solving for $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= -4.5x + 33 \\\\\n10 &= -4.5x + 33 \\\\\n- 23 &= -4.5x \\\\\n&= x \\mid \\approx 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, it takes approximately $5$ years for the car's value to drop to $\\[math]10\\,000$.\n\n**Note:** Since we're extrapolating (the point where $y=10$ is not within the original data range), our result *may* be unreliable." 13194139535987 17592186045417 false] [17592186096595 1074 "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny = mx+b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{{S}_{xx}},\\,b=\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m{:}$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(0-2)(35-24)+(1-2)(26-24) \\\\  & +(3-2)(19-24)+(4-2)(16-24) \\\\  & =(-2)(11)+(-1)(2)+(1)(-5)+(2)(-8) \\\\  & =-22-2-5-16 \\\\  & =-45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(0-2)^{2}+(1-2)^{2}+(3-2)^{2}+(4-2)^{2} \\\\  & =4+1+1+4 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Now, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm =-\\dfrac{45}{10} = -4.5.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =24-(-\\frac{9}{2})\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny = -4.5x+33\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate the required value by substituting $y=10$ into the equation of the trend line and solving for $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4.5x+33 \\\\ 10 & =-4.5x+33 \\\\ -23 & =-4.5x \\\\ x & ≈5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, it takes approximately $5$ years for the car's value to drop to $\\[math]10\\,000.$\n\n**Note:** Since we're extrapolating (the point where $y=10$ is not within the original data range), our result *may* be unreliable." 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096628 1038 17592186553515 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096628 1038 17592186553533 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096628 1038 17592186553588 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096629 1038 17592186553583 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096658 1038 17592186553580 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096753 1038 17592186553513 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096754 1038 17592186553526 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096754 1038 17592186553544 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096754 1038 17592186553573 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096755 1038 17592186553510 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096755 1038 17592186553512 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096822 1038 17592186553491 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096822 1038 17592186553502 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096822 1038 17592186553522 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096822 1038 17592186553568 13194139535987 17592186045417 true] [17592186096822 